# Event-source order storage

Order storage moves from CRUD tables to an append-only event log, because auditors must be able to replay any order's full history. We chose this over adding an audit table and over change data capture, since neither gives a replayable history of what the business intended, only of the rows that changed. Reversing this later would mean rebuilding every read model.

## Considered Options

- **Audit table next to the CRUD tables**: rejected. It records row changes, not domain intent, and it can drift from the real state.
- **Change data capture**: rejected for the same reason. It captures low-level row diffs, so you cannot replay them as business history.
- **Event-sourced log**: chosen.
